<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#system-ponto-riscado> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The graphic sign system of Brazilian Umbanda and Quimbanda, consisting of drawn points (pontos) associated with Orixás, Exus, and Pombagiras. Related to but distinct from Palo Monte firmás; developed in the Brazilian context with syncretic elements from African, Indigenous, and Spiritist sources."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#system-anaforuana> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Many Anaforuana signs are protected at initiated-only or no-access level by potencia authority. Researchers must obtain community approval before documenting or publishing specific signs."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#colorSignificance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ritual significance of colors used with this sign, where applicable. Initiated-only."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#func-sealing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sign closes or concludes a ceremony or seals a spiritual agreement."@en .
