<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#system-anaforuana> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The esoteric graphic script of the Abakuá society in Cuba, derived from Ejagham Nsibidi through enslaved Cross River practitioners. Anaforuana signs represent potencia territories, spiritual forces, and society knowledge. Among the most protected sign systems in the Afro-Atlantic world; specific signs are restricted to initiated members at specific grades. Related to but institutionally distinct from Nsibidi."@en .
