<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#surface-floor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Interior floor of a temple, hounfò, or ilé. The most common surface for Vodou vèvè."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#surface-cloth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fabric or cloth, particularly for Adinkra stamping and some Vodou ceremonial use."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#surface-water> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A body of water, basin, or liquid surface. Used in some healing and cooling ceremonies."@en .
